{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3021","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3021","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3021\",\"parent_revision\":\"756093114a8c18a80609456622efbef838fa7e8431938f0c13831dea12f6b1a7\",\"root_revision\":\"756093114a8c18a80609456622efbef838fa7e8431938f0c13831dea12f6b1a7\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nDiscovered 2026-08-19 while investigating why `/dh:work-backlog-item` still failed after PR #3005 merged and `/reload-plugins` was run.\\n\\nRoot cause: the `auto-sync-manifests` pre-commit hook (`.pre-commit-config.yaml`, entry `plugins/plugin-creator/scripts/auto_sync_manifests.py`) only fires on a local `git commit`. A PR merged via GitHub's squash-merge button/API never runs local hooks, so `plugin.json`'s version is never bumped for that merge \u2014 even though the plugin's actual content changed on `main`.\\n\\nConfirmed: `git show ba58d56d -- plugins/development-harness/.claude-plugin/plugin.json` (the #3005 merge commit) is an empty diff \u2014 the SKILL.md fix landed with zero version bump. Since `plugin.json` already said \\\"9.0.15\\\" (bumped by an earlier, unrelated local commit), the marketplace cache \u2014 keyed on version number \u2014 saw no delta and never re-fetched, so `/reload-plugins` correctly reported success while serving pre-fix content.\\n\\nThere is also no retroactive repair: running `auto_sync_manifests.py` directly against already-committed `main` reports \\\"No manifest updates needed\\\" regardless of whether a prior GitHub-merged commit should have bumped the version \u2014 the script only detects a live uncommitted diff, not a historical gap between a plugin's actual content and its declared version.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Every PR that changes files under a `plugins/{name}/` path bumps that plugin's `plugin.json` version before or as part of merging, regardless of merge method (squash via UI, `gh pr merge`, rebase, etc.) \u2014 likely via a required CI check (a GitHub Action) that either blocks the merge if the version wasn't bumped, or auto-bumps and pushes a version-bump commit as part of the merge/CI flow\\n- [ ] A retroactive audit mode exists (or is documented as intentionally out of scope) to detect plugins whose `plugin.json` version doesn't reflect their actual last-changed commit, so an already-missed bump like this one can be found and fixed without manual investigation\\n- [ ] The fix is validated by simulating a GitHub-side merge (not a local commit) that changes a plugin file, confirming the version bump lands\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on `/reload-plugins` to pick up plugin changes**, I want to **every merged plugin change to actually bump plugin.json's version**, so that **the marketplace cache reliably refreshes instead of silently serving stale content indefinitely**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Found via direct investigation (not guessed) while debugging why `/dh:work-backlog-item` still failed post-#3005-merge and post-`/reload-plugins`. Full evidence trail: `git show ba58d56d -- .../plugin.json` (empty diff), direct inspection of `~/.claude/plugins/cache/jamie-bitflight-skills/dh/9.0.15/` (stale content), and `auto_sync_manifests.py`'s own \\\"no updates needed\\\" response against already-stale committed state.\\n- **Related fix already applied**: PR #3020 manually bumps `dh`'s version to 9.0.16 to unblock this specific instance and corrects a related false claim in `.claude/rules/plugin-development.md` (that a full session restart, not `/reload-plugins`, was required \u2014 that claim was itself wrong since 2026-03-23).\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"0a093215dba7897830f00367106419b66ad4b17f8aeccbfeddc181b13dd24741\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPiOymw\"}"}